  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): Belongs as a member of INV-numat — the name-collision sub-finding (5 field names appearing on both edge.meta and node.meta with disjoint vocabularies) is the umbrella's exact shape (one name, multiple semantic axes). The zero-entropy sub-finding (17 fields) traces to three distinct shapes: dead-code-emitter (channel_kind='queue', protocol='ws' — field added during multi-mechanism design, only one mechanism shipped), defensive-flag (disambiguation_fallback=True only-when-populated), and single-emitter-constant (bridge_kind='ffi' because every bridge linker on hypergumbo's surface is FFI). dest_access_mode='read' as zero-entropy is also cross-evidence for INV-kudug — the access_mode subsystem is unhealthy. Candidate to split into three sub-items so each shape can resolve independently; alternatively absorb the name-collision half into INV-numat and keep this item focused on entropy."  # e706
- op: discuss  # bca2
  at: '2026-06-07T06:42:01Z'  # bca2
  by: agent  # bca2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bca2
  clock: 4  # bca2
  nonce: bca2  # bca2
  message: "Dogfood fold (member F147.A1-a, split from F147.A1), reproduces on the frozen substrate. Refinement of this row's symptom (1) \"channel_kind='queue' (103 occurrences)\" constant-value-only finding, sharpened to the value-space realizability gap: the documented channel_kind value-space is {ipc, websocket, queue, message_bus, crdt} but only the message-queue linker stamps channel_kind, and it always emits queue. The other four documented discriminator values have no producing path that reaches the output. Scope: channel_kind present on exactly 103 edges, all value=queue (kafka 85, rabbitmq 12, sqs 4, redis 2); 0 edges carry the other four values. Consequence: branch arms for the four never-emitted values are dead; an agent classifying inter-process/inter-service communication can only ever see \"queue,\" under-reporting IPC, WebSocket, message-bus, and CRDT couplings. Resolves with this row's stated fix (symptom 1: \"Either the field should be derived from origin/edge.type, or other-value cases need linker support\") — the websocket-linker WS-send path in particular should stamp channel_kind=websocket (see the related WS-bypass row WI-bumug). Folded here rather than filed new because the mechanism (linker only emits one channel_kind mechanism) and fix are the same as this row's symptom (1). Cross-ref WI-bumug (WS bypasses channel_kind entirely)."  # bca2
